// BT-3701 / ADR 0130 §2: `self hasField:` in an inheritable class method runs
// with the *receiver* class as `ClassSelf`, so a parent without class
// variables still answers for a subclass that declares one. Only a
// direct-called method (sealed class, `class sealed` method) has no
// `ClassSelf`; see direct_dispatch_stateless.bt.

Object subclass: HasFieldProbeBase

  class probe => self hasField: #n

  class probeInBlock => [self hasField: #n] value
